<p>Russian missile and drone strikes hit several Ukrainian cities including Kyiv, Odesa and Dnipro, killing at least 22 people and injuring more than 131, according to Ukrainian officials and local reporting. The attacks were described by multiple outlets as Russia&#x27;s deadliest aerial assault in months or its worst attack of the year so far. Ukraine&#x27;s air force said Russia launched 659 drones and 44 missiles in the barrage, while Russia&#x27;s military said it had targeted Ukrainian military and energy facilities. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the strikes showed Moscow did not merit any easing of sanctions, while Kyiv&#x27;s European partners condemned the attacks on civilians, underscoring how far any negotiated end to the war still appears to be.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qevG6PtCslJfH0xTFNzv5kgzZA5PGGc6QiUFEoh1ytrilQTxVbIN8eGTJ_SNSYL_LSP12PBOBBSHtRpkgBwZztJpJmACGeiktypgXfBxl60P' alt='Ukrainian rescuers work at the site of heavily damaged buildings following a Russian air attack in Dnipro on April 16, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Russian losses: Russian officials said Ukrainian strikes killed two people in Russia after the truce period.</li><li>Talks stalled: The mass attack came with efforts to end the war still stalled more than four years after Russia&#x27;s full-scale invasion of Ukraine began.</li><li>Rescue work: Journalists in Kyiv reported loud explosions overnight and smoke over the city at dawn as emergency crews responded at damaged residential sites.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelensky: The Ukrainian president called for a minute of silence during a visit to a church in the Netherlands and argued the attack showed Russia should not receive sanctions relief. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992442/russian-strikes-kill-19-across-ukraine'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Russian military: Moscow said it had carried out a massive strike against what it described as Ukrainian military and energy targets, rather than civilian sites. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992442/russian-strikes-kill-19-across-ukraine'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Antonio Costa: The European Council president accused Russia of choosing to deliberately terrorise civilians and called the strikes a horrendous attack against civilian targets. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992442/russian-strikes-kill-19-across-ukraine'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cm29plylqnvo'>Russia launches deadliest aerial attack in months, killing 18 in Ukraine</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/russian-strikes-kill-17-across-ukraine-in-worst-attack-this-year'>Russian strikes kill 17 across Ukraine in worst attack this year</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-russian-strikes-across-ukraine-many-more-injured/a-76803204'>Several killed in Russian strikes across Ukraine, many more injured</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1992442/russian-strikes-kill-19-across-ukraine'>Russian strikes kill 19 across Ukraine</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://kyivindependent.com/at-least-21-killed-131-injured-in-russian-strikes-across-ukraine-over-past-day/'>Russian missile and drone strikes across Ukraine, including on Kyiv and Odesa, kill at least 22 people and wound more than 131 others.</a> - kyivindependent.com</li></ul>